From 217a3022dd4a5135d34354fc7da777a690f07705 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: eileenthg <40307498+eileenthg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 23:48:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] Fix broad systemic API changes surfaced by compileJava:
 tooltip context, effects, tiers, codecs

- appendHoverText(ItemStack, @Nullable Level, List<Component>, TooltipFlag) -> (ItemStack,
  Item.TooltipContext, List<Component>, TooltipFlag) across all 11 of our own Item subclasses
  that weren't touched by the mechanical Forge-import pass (DItem, DConsumableItem, DrinkItem,
  CompatItem, CompatBlockItem, FurnaceFuelItem, DKnifeItem, ChorusMuffinItem, DBoozeItem,
  FermentedEnderNectarItem, RockCandyItem) - confirmed against FD's own ConsumableItem.java.
- MobEffectInstance's constructors now require Holder<MobEffect> instead of raw MobEffect;
  centralized the fix in Util.addEffect() (wraps via BuiltInRegistries.MOB_EFFECT.wrapAsHolder)
  and fixed ChorusMuffinItem's direct hasEffect/removeEffect calls the same way.
- FoodProperties#getEffects() returning List<Pair<MobEffectInstance,Float>> is now
  effects() returning List<FoodProperties.PossibleEffect> (.effect()/.probability()) - fixed in
  Util.getFoodEffects and in SlicedMelonBlock/SlicedMiniMelonBlock/SlicedGourdBlock's
  bite-eating effect loops (the latter also still had the old isEdible()/3-arg
  FoodData.eat(Item,ItemStack,LivingEntity) bugs from the same root cause, missed earlier since
  it has no Forge imports of its own).
- FoodProperties.Builder#saturationMod -> saturationModifier (58 call sites in Nutrition.java
  plus 5 compat food-value files).
- BlockBehaviour.Properties#copy(Block) -> ofFullCopy(BlockBehaviour) (DelightfulBlocks,
  DelightfulMilkshakeCauldronBlock, DPieBlock, WildSalmonberriesBlock).
- ItemStack#hurtAndBreak(int, LivingEntity, Consumer<LivingEntity>) is gone; replaced with the
  new hurtAndBreak(int, LivingEntity, EquipmentSlot) + LivingEntity.getSlotForHand(hand) across
  7 call sites, matching FD's own convention.
- Vanilla's MelonBlock class removal already handled; BushBlock now re-abstracts
  Block#codec(), so CantaloupePlantBlock and SalmonberryBushBlock (the only two direct
  BushBlock subclasses) each gained a simpleCodec()-based codec() override - verified other
  bases we extend (FlowerBlock via WildCropBlock, PieBlock, CabinetBlock) already provide a
  concrete codec() so no other subclasses need one.
- Tier#getLevel() was removed from the interface entirely (no numeric mining level concept
  anymore); DelightfulTiers's own custom getLevel() field is harmless as a non-override, but
  the vanilla Tiers.IRON/DIAMOND/NETHERITE.getLevel() call sites used to derive modded tier
  stats don't exist anymore - replaced with the equivalent literal constants (2/3/4). Added the
  new required Tier#getIncorrectBlocksForDrops() override (returns
  BlockTags.INCORRECT_FOR_WOODEN_TOOL as a harmless default; knife block-breaking eligibility is
  handled separately via ModTags.Blocks.MINEABLE_WITH_KNIFE, not tier level).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
